---
description: Shared engineering workflow for this repository
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow the canonical shared instructions in @Engineering/ENGINEERING.md before engineering work. Preserve and follow applicable repository-specific instructions too. Open the file if its content has not been loaded. Reusable task procedures are discoverable under `.agents/skills/`.

Work on an implementation task in its own Git worktree and branch, created or safely reused before the first edit, and never modify another agent's worktree.

Every session that changes this repository must finish the mandatory end-of-session protocol before it stops, and report each result: (1) review the complete diff for correctness, unrelated changes, and exposed secrets; (2) run the relevant tests and report their actual results, never presenting a failing or skipped check as a pass; (3) commit the reviewed, claimed changes with a descriptive message; (4) push the task's own feature branch; (5) create or update exactly one pull request for that branch — ready for review when complete and passing, otherwise a draft documenting the blockers under a `## Blockers` heading; (6) update the associated GitHub issue and Project board status, or report the exact blocked operation; (7) hand off completed work, remaining work, test results, blockers, the pull request URL, and the engineering concepts involved.

A session with no repository changes performs step 7 only and creates no pull request. Preserve unfinished work as commits plus a draft pull request. Never merge your own pull request, force-push, discard changes, or bypass failing checks. Use `/start-task` and `/finish-task`, and verify with `pwsh -File Engineering/scripts/end-session.ps1 -Repository <task-worktree>`. Cursor cannot enforce this automatically at session end; follow it yourself and state anything the scripts could not verify.
